WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The intelligence lifecycle turns a broad concern into a repeatable analytical process.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
It begins with requirements: the specific questions the work must answer,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
the decision it will support, the permitted scope, and the deadline.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.190
Clear requirements prevent endless collection and reduce unnecessary privacy impact.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.995
Collection identifies and obtains relevant public material using approved methods.

00:00:19.995 --> 00:00:23.995
A collection plan maps each requirement to likely source categories, priorities,

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:25.000
and stopping conditions.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.800
Analysts should avoid gathering sensitive personal information simply because it is

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.240
technically visible.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.985
Processing converts collected material into a usable form.

00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:36.245
This may include organizing records, normalizing dates,

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:40.165
extracting text from permitted documents, translating content, removing duplicates,

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.180
and preserving source metadata.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.265
Processing should not erase provenance or uncertainty.

00:00:44.265 --> 00:00:47.990
Analysis compares observations, tests explanations, identifies patterns,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.000
and assesses significance.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.995
Validation checks source origin, timing, internal consistency, and corroboration.

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:57.640
Analysts should actively look for disconfirming evidence instead of selecting only

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.245
material that supports an early theory.

00:00:59.245 --> 00:01:01.985
Reporting communicates findings for the intended audience.

00:01:01.985 --> 00:01:05.260
A useful report answers the requirement, cites supporting evidence,

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.019
distinguishes fact from inference, states confidence, and identifies important gaps.

00:01:09.019 --> 00:01:12.255
Detail should match the reader's role and the consequences of action.

00:01:12.255 --> 00:01:14.195
Feedback closes the lifecycle.

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:16.990
Decision-makers may refine the requirement, request clarification,

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.920
or identify new questions.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.995
Analysts can also improve source selection and documentation based on review.

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:26.880
The lifecycle is iterative, but it remains bounded by purpose, authority, time,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.840
and proportionality.
